==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Razorback]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
**2 [[Two Can]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
**3 [[Tackey]]s spawn, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage might be tricky due to the pushing power of the two Razorbacks alongside the Tackeys and Two Cans sniping some of your backline if they get close enough. As always, in any stage that contains Razorback, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] is essential to fighting the Razorbacks. [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Frolicking Nono]] is an incredible meatshield against Darks, but if you don't own her, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and/or [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] are great alternatives. For the attackers, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] is a go-to, especially if you have his Wave Talents to reach the Two Cans and Tackeys as well as getting rid of hordes of Dark Doges. Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] is incredible as well, particularly if they Weaken the Razorbacks. If one happens to own [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], his Wave will also help tremendously with killing the backlines and Dark Doges as long as the Razorbacks aren't pushing too quickly. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] will help deal some extra damage on the Two Cans too. Overall, don't overthink this stage, especially if you've completed [[Taste of Success (Merciless)|Taste of Success]]. Just bring the best [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Darks]] you have, which you should have great options up until this point.

